# The image builds the library from source in /root/sb2l/build. Anything a
# local build left behind must stay out of the context: COPY would otherwise
# bring a CMakeCache.txt naming a directory which does not exist in the image,
# and cmake refuses to reuse a cache generated somewhere else. The build then
# fails on a machine where the library was compiled first, which is what the
# README tells the reader to do.
build/
examples/build/

# .git is deliberately kept: the image runs `git submodule update --init` to
# fetch SymEngine and Dear ImGui.

# Editor and run-time leftovers.
.vscode/
imgui.ini
